<urn:anqr:known-limitation:qrartefactcreation-codec> <urn:usf:predicate:constraintReason> "The facet requires that a produced artefact decodes to the requested payload, which can only be satisfied by a working QR codec: Reed-Solomon over GF(256), matrix placement, finder and alignment patterns, and a decoder. The capability convention forbids any import outside the Node standard library, so that codec must be written from scratch in one module. A bounded worker model repeatedly produced the option and validation surface around a non-functional codec that decodes to the empty string; aimed repair with the real decode-mismatch assertion did not close it. This is the implementation mathematics the programme charter deliberately excludes from semantics, surfacing as a genuine realisation limit rather than a defect." <urn:anqr:graph:known-limitations> .
<urn:anqr:known-limitation:qrartefactcreation-codec> <urn:usf:predicate:resolutionOptions> "Escalate this one capability to a frontier route capable of a full codec; or amend the convention to permit one audited QR library for this capability; or leave it open. The operator accepted it as a documented hard tail on 2026-09-02." <urn:anqr:graph:known-limitations> .
<urn:anqr:known-limitation:qrartefactcreation-codec> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "This record documents an unsatisfied capability. It does not mark the capability satisfied, and the facet evaluator continues to report its facets as unsatisfied from executed evidence. It excludes them only from this directive's completion condition, auditably and with a reason." <urn:anqr:graph:known-limitations> .
